-- GAME ----------------------------------------------------------------------
  Title       Cybernoid - The Fighting Machine
  Publisher   Hewson Consultants, 1988
  Version     1.1

-- YOU NEED ------------------------------------------------------------------
  Your own copy of the original game, saved beside this patch:

  File        Cybernoid - The Fighting Machine (1988)(Hewson
              Consultants)(128K).z80
  MD5         92ad5a23acfe06f0756ae2d503ab31cc

  The patch carries none of the game's code. It only works with that exact
  dump, under that name or any other: anything else is refused, with a
  message naming the file it wants.

-- WHAT IT DOES --------------------------------------------------------------
  Moving figures become Next hardware sprites, so they keep their own colours
  and no longer take on the scenery's (colour clash). Game logic is unchanged.

  Colours     Default (the game's own) plus: Enhanced, chosen on the menu, off
              by default.
  Enhanced    The Spec256 conversion's colours on the figures: the ship,
              enemies, weapons and effects in fuller colour over the game's
              own scenery, as approved for the earlier build. A painted set,
              colourist not named.

  Pace        original

  Changes     1.1: the 128K release with AY music; the original's pace kept by
              a limiter; works on NextZXOS v2.10; verified 128K cheats; the
              approved Enhanced colours unchanged

  Note        128K release with AY sound. Original colours with clash removed
              by default; approved Enhanced colours optional and off by
              default. Known issues: Very heavy debris can exceed the
              available small-figure slots, as in the approved earlier build.
              The loader displays the first eight trainers; additional
              verified trainers are host-tool options only. Missing: hardware
              testing, natural full-game completion, and unsupported archive
              trainer variants.

-- MENU ----------------------------------------------------------------------
   1  Infinite lives
   2  Infinite weapon stock
   3  Immunity
   4  Start with 99 lives
   5  No enemies
   6  No guns
   7  No tunnel aliens
   8  No snakes
   9  No rockets
  10  No flying aliens
  11  Sound off
  12  Keep backshot on death
  13  Keep satellite on death

  The archive's POKEs, checked against this 128K release and translated where
  they differ; Sound off uses the game's own sound-off entry points, as the
  archive's address is wrong for this version. Five more tested cheats (No
  rockets, No flying aliens, Sound off, Keep backshot on death, Keep satellite
  on death) are in the patch but beyond the loader's eight cheat lines.

